<% content_for :title, "Install Knowledge Vault · Slack" %>
<div class="kv-page">
  <div class="kv-page-header">
    <div class="kv-heading-group">
      <h1>Install Knowledge Vault</h1>
      <p>Internal AI search over your company docs — in Slack and in the app.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="kv-badge-row">
      <div class="kv-pill">
        <span class="kv-pill-dot"></span>
        Slack app
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-install-hero">
    <p class="kv-install-lead">
      <strong>Found Knowledge Vault on the Slack Marketplace?</strong> Sign up here to connect the bot to your workspace. You’ll get a private backoffice where you upload documents and manage the integration. <strong>If your workspace is already connected</strong>, sign up or log in and connect Slack — you’ll be added to your team’s organization automatically.
    </p>
    <ol class="kv-install-steps">
      <li>
        <span class="kv-step-num">1</span>
        <span><strong>Create an account</strong> — we’ll set up your organization and make you the admin.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="kv-step-num">2</span>
        <span><strong>Connect Slack</strong> — from Integrations, connect your Slack workspace so the bot can answer questions from your knowledge base.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="kv-step-num">3</span>
        <span><strong>Upload docs &amp; ask</strong> — add documents, then ask questions in the app or by mentioning the bot in Slack.</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="kv-install-cta">
      <%= link_to "Add to Slack", slack_install_path, class: "kv-primary-button" %>
      <%= link_to "Create account", new_user_registration_path, class: "kv-secondary-button" %>
      <%= link_to "Log in", new_user_session_path, class: "kv-secondary-button" %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-soft-divider"></div>
  <p class="kv-meta-text kv-meta-muted">
    Need help? See our <%= link_to "Support", support_path %> page or <%= link_to "Privacy policy", privacy_path %>.
  </p>
</div>
